Package: jsdiffr
Type: Package
Title: Text and Sequence Diffing Ported from 'jsdiff'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kyle", "Haynes", email = "kyle@kylehaynes.com.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kevin", "Decker", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of the original 'jsdiff' JavaScript library (https://github.com/kpdecker/jsdiff)"))
Description: A faithful R port of the 'jsdiff' JavaScript library. Computes
    differences between two pieces of text or two sequences at the level of
    characters, words, lines, sentences, CSS tokens, 'JSON' values, or arbitrary
    arrays, using Myers' O(ND) difference algorithm. The core diff loop is
    implemented in C++ for speed on large inputs. Also provides the full 'jsdiff'
    patch suite (create, apply, parse, and reverse unified diff patches),
    converters to XML and the Google diff-match-patch format, and helpers for
    rendering diffs as coloured console output or HTML for use in 'shiny' apps.
